Method 1: Using the MinIO Console (Recommended)

Log in to the MinIO Console:

http://192.168.1.198:9501

(or :9001 if you're still using the default console port)

In the left menu, go to:

Identity → Users
Click Create User.
Enter:

Access Key (username), for example:

myapp

Secret Key (password), for example:

MyAppSecret@123456
Assign the readwrite policy (or a more restrictive custom policy if appropriate).
Click Create.

Now use these credentials in your application:

Endpoint   : http://192.168.1.198:9500
Access Key : myapp
Secret Key : MyAppSecret@123456
Bucket     : bariflo-storage
Method 2: Using the MinIO Client (mc)

Configure an alias for your server:

mc alias set local http://192.168.1.198:9500 Bariflo Bariflomino@2401

Create a user:

mc admin user add local myapp MyAppSecret@123456

Attach the built-in read/write policy:

mc admin policy attach local readwrite --user myapp

List users:

mc admin user list local
Example application configuration
MINIO_ENDPOINT=http://192.168.1.198:9500
MINIO_ACCESS_KEY=myapp
MINIO_SECRET_KEY=MyAppSecret@123456
MINIO_BUCKET=bariflo-storage
Note about the root account

Your current root credentials are:

Root User     : Bariflo
Root Password : Bariflomino@2401

These are intended for administration. It's better to create separate users for applications so you can rotate credentials or limit permissions without affecting the administrative account.
